				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance submodules — comments shim and extension scan fix\n\nAdvance Cocoon, Mountain, Output, Rest, and Wind submodules to complete the registry-backed vscode.comments namespace shim in Cocoon and fix user extension discovery on extension cache hits in Mountain.\n\nCocoon replaces the stock no-op stub for `vscode.comments` with a dynamic import of a `CommentsNamespace` factory in Source/Services/Handler/VscodeAPI/Comments/Namespace.ts. Each CommentController now owns a Map-backed thread registry keyed on `UriStr:Line:Char` with mutable thread state. Registration is idempotent. The RouteManifest is regenerated with three newly exposed Mountain RPC methods (setStatusBarText, Task.Terminate, terminate_task), bringing the count from 137 to 140.\n\nMountain adds a supplementary live-scan phase on extension cache hits that re-uses `Registry.GetExtensionScanPaths()` filtered through `Scanner::IsUserExtensionScanPath`, ensuring VSIX-installed extensions at `~/.fiddee/extensions` and `~/.land/extensions` are discovered even when the bundled cache is fresh. The missing `TierCommandEventBroadcast` entry is also added to Info.plist.\n\nOutput, Rest, and Wind receive non-functional updates — regenerated VLQ mappings, rebuilt binary artifact, and daily catalog version date bump respectively.",
			"SHA": "fe0afd794b553b3a6952d0123c2aa3911d3e1e65"
		},
